+// Composites one surface's newest frame into an arbitrary screen-space quad,
+// which is how a CEF page ends up on a television in the world.
+//
+// This lives here, next to `Draw`, and not in `WorldOverlay` on purpose. It is
+// the same operation as `Draw` performs -- pick the GPU ring slot or the CPU
+// upload, queue an `AddImageQuad` into the current frame's background draw list,
+// wrap the whole thing in the premultiplied-alpha pipeline state -- and the two
+// must not drift apart. `Draw` decides the texture; nothing outside this file
+// should be handling a descriptor handle.
+//
+// `aCorners` is eight floats: top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left, in
+// the caller's pixel space, already projected by a game-thread producer. `aAlpha`
+// is 0..255, applied as a tint so a producer's own distance fade reaches the
+// pixels rather than being simulated by a smaller quad.
+//
+// Returns false, drawing nothing, when the surface is missing, hidden, not yet
+// ready, or has never been painted. That is deliberately the same predicate
+// `Draw` uses, so "the TV is blank" and "the page is blank" stay distinguishable
+// through `webui.status`.
+[[nodiscard]] bool DrawSurfaceQuad(WebUI::SurfaceId aSurface, const float (&aCorners)[8], uint8_t aAlpha);
 // Once per swapchain Present, whether or not the overlay drew: paces the host's
